Notes on A
- The 24 warnings of the +define+SYNTHESIS lint are UNUSEDSIGNAL (bus_rsp_last_i, read only by
  the caches' existing `ifndef SYNTHESIS assertions; req_off[2:0] in sigil_mbus_axi4). They are
  main's own: the same 17 runs on a `git archive eeaa332` copy give byte-identical diagnostics on
  both Verilators. `make lint` itself does not define SYNTHESIS and is clean (0 warnings).
- "perf identifiers 0" = with SYNTHESIS defined, the preprocessed sigil_cpu contains no perf_*
  or PE_STK* identifier at all; the synthesis views of every flow's define set are byte-identical
  to main eeaa332 (synth_view_diff.sh). Nothing new can reach a netlist.
- The 4 "differing lines" of the PASS-line comparison are command echoes that contain the
  worktree path (~/wt/main-eeaa332 vs ~/wt/56-gates); every TB PASS / EXAMPLE PASS line,
  cycle counts included, is identical to main's.
- The core-test coverage line above (54.00%, 3727/6840) is not comparable with main's
  reference, because this run did `make test` first and its crypto unit TBs add 7 coverage
  files (cov_cryptotop/ecfield/hashstream/keccak/sha256/sha512 and cov_rvtest from
  riscv-tests). Section B compares like with like.
- ACT: the only failure is the known PA0 waiver PMPSm_cfg_A_tor_zero-00 (18,024 cycles). Against
  docs/evidence/act-core-w0-stack-2026-10-20.csv: the same 2,578 tests, the same verdicts and
  identical cycle counts for all 2,578.

